{"thought":"I’ve checked the active structure, palette, navigation, typography, responsive, theme, and footer rules. I’ll now build a complete single-file site with all five profiles, their portraits, a synthesized future-of-engineering section, and an accessible persistent theme toggle.","action":"write_site","args":{}}```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
  <title>Team Thoughtful Systems | Agentic SE Lab</title>
  <script>
    (function () {
      try {
        const saved = localStorage.getItem("upb-theme");
        const theme = saved === "light" || saved === "dark"
          ? saved
          : (window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches ? "dark" : "light");
        document.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme;
      } catch (_) {
        document.documentElement.dataset.theme =
          window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches ? "dark" : "light";
      }
    }());
  </script>
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: light;
      --bg: #FFF8E7;
      --text: #1D1D1F;
      --secondary: #5A5A5F;
      --card: #FFFFFF;
      --accent: #A64D35;
      --accent-strong: #753322;
      --accent-soft: #F2E2D2;
      --line: #E8DDCB;
      --shadow: 0 18px 45px rgba(68, 47, 25, .08);
      --soft-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(68, 47, 25, .06);
      --chip: #F7EFE2;
      --quote: #8B432E;
      --hero-wash: #F6EBD8;
      --focus: #A64D35;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
    }

    :root[data-theme="dark"] {
      color-scheme: dark;
      --bg: #14142B;
      --text: #F4F1DE;
      --secondary: #B8B5A7;
      --card: #1F1F3D;
      --accent: #E6A47C;
      --accent-strong: #F1BD98;
      --accent-soft: #34304B;
      --line: #3A3855;
      --shadow: 0 18px 45px rgba(0, 0, 0, .2);
      --soft-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, .15);
      --chip: #292944;
      --quote: #F0B28B;
      --hero-wash: #20203B;
      --focus: #F0B28B;
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; }

    html {
      background: var(--bg);
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      min-width: 0;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.65;
      transition: background-color .25s ease, color .25s ease;
    }

    a { color: inherit; }

    a:focus-visible, button:focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--focus);
      outline-offset: 4px;
    }

    .shell {
      width: min(1120px, calc(100% - 3rem));
      margin-inline: auto;
    }

    .site-header {
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
      padding: 1.5rem 0 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      background:
        radial-gradient(ellipse at 83% 4%, var(--hero-wash), transparent 36%),
        var(--bg);
    }

    .header-top {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    .brand {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: .75rem;
      color: var(--text);
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .brand-mark {
      display: grid;
      width: 2.65rem;
      aspect-ratio: 1;
      place-items: center;
      border-radius: .9rem;
      background: var(--accent);
      color: var(--bg);
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      font-weight: 850;
      letter-spacing: -.08em;
      box-shadow: var(--soft-shadow);
    }

    .brand-name {
      font-size: .92rem;
      font-weight: 760;
      letter-spacing: -.025em;
    }

    #theme-toggle {
      display: inline-grid;
      width: 2.8rem;
      height: 2.8rem;
      place-items: center;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--card);
      color: var(--text);
      box-shadow: var(--soft-shadow);
      cursor: pointer;
      font: inherit;
      font-size: 1.15rem;
      transition: transform .2s ease, background-color .2s ease;
    }

    #theme-toggle:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); }

    .intro {
      max-width: 760px;
      padding: 4.3rem 0 2.6rem;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: .55rem;
      margin: 0 0 .9rem;
      color: var(--accent-strong);
      font-size: .76rem;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: .14em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .eyebrow::before {
      width: 1.5rem;
      height: 2px;
      background: var(--accent);
      content: "";
    }

    h1, h2, h3, p { margin-top: 0; }

    h1 {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      font-size: clamp(2.65rem, 6vw, 5.45rem);
      font-weight: 780;
      letter-spacing: -.075em;
      line-height: .99;
    }

    .tagline {
      max-width: 630px;
      margin-bottom: 0;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.25rem);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .site-nav {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: .35rem;
      padding: 0 0 1.15rem;
    }

    .site-nav a {
      padding: .58rem .9rem;
      border-radius: 999px;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: .88rem;
      font-weight: 650;
      text-decoration: none;
      transition: color .2s ease, background-color .2s ease;
    }

    .site-nav a:hover {
      background: var(--accent-soft);
      color: var(--text);
    }

    main { padding-bottom: 2rem; }

    .section {
      padding-block: 5rem;
      scroll-margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }

    .section-heading {
      display: flex;
      align-items: end;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 2rem;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .section-heading h2 {
      margin-bottom: .4rem;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.15rem);
      font-weight: 760;
      letter-spacing: -.06em;
      line-height: 1.1;
    }

    .section-heading p {
      max-width: 560px;
      margin-bottom: 0;
      color: var(--secondary);
    }

    .team-note {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      padding: .52rem .8rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 999px;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: .78rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .member-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1.2rem;
    }

    .member-card {
      min-width: 0;
      overflow: hidden;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 1.25rem;
      background: var(--card);
      box-shadow: var(--soft-shadow);
      transition: transform .2s ease, box-shadow .2s ease, background-color .25s ease;
    }

    .member-card:hover {
      transform: translateY(-3px);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    .member-top {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 1.05rem;
      padding: 1.2rem 1.3rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    .portrait {
      width: 5.2rem;
      height: 5.2rem;
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      border: 3px solid var(--accent-soft);
      border-radius: 1rem;
      background: var(--hero-wash);
      object-fit: cover;
    }

    .member-name {
      margin: 0 0 .2rem;
      font-size: 1.35rem;
      font-weight: 760;
      letter-spacing: -.04em;
      line-height: 1.2;
    }

    .study {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: .87rem;
    }

    .member-body { padding: 1.2rem 1.3rem 1.35rem; }

    .member-field + .member-field { margin-top: 1rem; }

    .field-label {
      margin: 0 0 .38rem;
      color: var(--accent-strong);
      font-size: .7rem;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: .11em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .member-field p:not(.field-label) {
      margin-bottom: 0;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: .9rem;
      line-height: 1.65;
    }

    .interest-list {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: .42rem;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;
    }

    .interest-list li {
      padding: .28rem .62rem;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: var(--chip);
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: .77rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .hot-take {
      padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
      border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
      border-radius: 0 .8rem .8rem 0;
      background: var(--accent-soft);
      color: var(--quote) !important;
      font-size: .95rem !important;
      font-weight: 680;
      letter-spacing: -.015em;
    }

    .future-section {
      padding: 4.2rem 0 4.5rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      background: var(--hero-wash);
    }

    .future-intro {
      max-width: 770px;
      margin-bottom: 2.2rem;
    }

    .future-intro h2 {
      margin-bottom: .9rem;
      font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 4.15rem);
      font-weight: 770;
      letter-spacing: -.07em;
      line-height: 1.05;
    }

    .future-intro > p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .future-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .future-card {
      padding: 1.35rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 1rem;
      background: var(--card);
      box-shadow: var(--soft-shadow);
    }

    .future-number {
      display: grid;
      width: 2.25rem;
      height: 2.25rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      place-items: center;
      border-radius: .75rem;
      background: var(--accent-soft);
      color: var(--accent-strong);
      font-size: .8rem;
      font-weight: 850;
    }

    .future-card h3 {
      margin-bottom: .55rem;
      font-size: 1.04rem;
      letter-spacing: -.025em;
    }

    .future-card p {
      margin-bottom: 0;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: .89rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .closing-thought {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 1.5rem;
      margin-top: 1.3rem;
      padding: 1.2rem 1.4rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 1rem;
      background: var(--card);
    }

    .closing-thought p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: .95rem;
      font-weight: 620;
    }

    .closing-thought span {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      color: var(--accent-strong);
      font-size: .77rem;
      font-weight: 780;
      letter-spacing: .08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    footer {
      padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
      color: var(--secondary);
      text-align: center;
      font-size: .8rem;
    }

    footer p { margin: 0; }

    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .shell { width: calc(100% - 2rem); }

      .site-header { padding-top: 1rem; }

      .header-top {
        align-items: flex-start;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: .6rem;
        padding-right: 3.4rem;
      }

      #theme-toggle {
        position: absolute;
        top: 1rem;
        right: 1rem;
      }

      .intro { padding: 3.25rem 0 2rem; }

      .site-nav {
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: flex-start;
        gap: .05rem;
        padding-bottom: .8rem;
      }

      .site-nav a { padding: .48rem .65rem; }

      .section { padding-block: 3.5rem; }

      .section-heading {
        align-items: flex-start;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: .85rem;
      }

      .member-grid,
      .future-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }

      .team-note { white-space: normal; }

      .future-section { padding: 3.5rem 0; }

      .closing-thought {
        align-items: flex-start;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: .55rem;
      }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      *, *::before, *::after {
        scroll-behavior: auto !important;
        animation-duration: .01ms !important;
        animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
        transition-duration: .01ms !important;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="header-top">
        <a class="brand" href="#team" aria-label="Thoughtful Systems team home">
          <span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">TS</span>
          <span class="brand-name">Thoughtful Systems</span>
        </a>
        <button id="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch to night mode">☾</button>
      </div>

      <div class="intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Agentic Software Engineering Lab</p>
        <h1>Good software starts with good questions.</h1>
        <p class="tagline">We’re five computer science students exploring how to build dependable systems without losing sight of the people who use them.</p>
      </div>

      <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href="#team">Meet the team</a>
        <a href="#future-of-se">The future of software engineering</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="section shell" id="team" aria-labelledby="team-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Curious by nature</p>
          <h2 id="team-title">Meet the team</h2>
          <p>Different interests, shared curiosity—and a healthy respect for the bugs that make it past the first build.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="team-note">5 people · many points of view</span>
      </div>

      <div class="member-grid">
        <article class="member-card">
          <div class="member-top">
            <img class="portrait" src="{{image:Mohammad.png}}" alt="Mohammad">
            <div>
              <h3 class="member-name">Mohammad</h3>
              <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science · 1st semester</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="member-body">
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">Into</p>
              <ul class="interest-list"><li>Full-stack development</li><li>Gaming</li></ul>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">A little known fact</p>
              <p>I’ll patiently sit through a 40-hour story-driven game with zero skips, but waiting 30 seconds for a build pipeline to finish tests my entire sanity.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">AI in engineering today</p>
              <p>AI is unmatched for boilerplate and syntax lookups, but can hallucinate subtle logical flaws that make debugging twice as tedious. It speeds up typing without genuinely understanding architecture or context. Right now, it works best as an eager junior developer whose every commit needs thorough code review.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">Looking 5–10 years ahead</p>
              <p>The core job will shift from typing code to specifying requirements, edge cases, and architectural constraints. Autonomous agents may handle boilerplate; engineering value will center on verification, fault tolerance, and knowing what to build.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">Hot take</p>
              <p class="hot-take">“AI doesn’t make bad developers good; it just helps them generate catastrophic technical debt at record speed.”</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <div class="member-top">
            <img class="portrait" src="{{image:Nithya.png}}" alt="Nithya">
            <div>
              <h3 class="member-name">Nithya</h3>
              <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science · 7th semester, thesis stage</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="member-body">
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">Into</p>
              <ul class="interest-list"><li>Distributed systems</li><li>Cloud architecture</li><li>Badminton</li><li>Board games</li></ul>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">A little known fact</p>
              <p>I have rewritten my thesis abstract more times than I have recompiled my actual code.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">AI in engineering today</p>
              <p>AI assistants are fantastic productivity multipliers for well-understood domains and boilerplate, but break down in complex legacy enterprise codebases. They can be confidently wrong about synchronization and concurrency. AI is a fast copilot—but you cannot let it navigate without senior oversight.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">Looking 5–10 years ahead</p>
              <p>Engineering will center on systems integration, prompt-driven formal verification, and distributed consensus rather than routine feature programming. Junior roles may evolve into system orchestration, where failure modes and domain invariants matter more than memorizing library APIs.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">Hot take</p>
              <p class="hot-take">“AI autocomplete hasn’t eliminated bugs; it has just made them compile much faster.”</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <div class="member-top">
            <img class="portrait" src="{{image:Rafee.png}}" alt="Rafee">
            <div>
              <h3 class="member-name">Rafee</h3>
              <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science · 1st semester</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="member-body">
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">Into</p>
              <ul class="interest-list"><li>Frontend UI/UX</li><li>React / Next.js</li><li>Table tennis</li><li>Photography</li></ul>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">A little known fact</p>
              <p>I judge coffee shops entirely by their Wi-Fi stability and latency to GitHub.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">AI in engineering today</p>
              <p>From a fresh developer perspective, AI is an unbelievable interactive tutor that demystifies obscure compiler errors in seconds. But relying on it too early creates an illusion of competence: you can understand the output without understanding the mechanics beneath it.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">Looking 5–10 years ahead</p>
              <p>Natural language and intent-driven wireframes may compile directly into accessible, responsive interfaces. Frontend engineers could focus more on user empathy, accessibility, and high-performance client-side state than on fighting CSS layouts.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">Hot take</p>
              <p class="hot-take">“If you can’t debug code without an LLM, you are the copilot, not the agent.”</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <div class="member-top">
            <img class="portrait" src="{{image:Raghvendra.png}}" alt="Raghvendra">
            <div>
              <h3 class="member-name">Raghvendra</h3>
              <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science · 3rd semester</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="member-body">
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">Into</p>
              <ul class="interest-list"><li>ML infrastructure</li><li>Data engineering</li><li>Hiking</li><li>Chess</li></ul>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">A little known fact</p>
              <p>I will spend 4 hours automating a manual 5-minute task, and call it an investment.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">AI in engineering today</p>
              <p>Current LLMs are incredible for rapid prototyping and translating business logic into SQL or boilerplate endpoints. However, they lack deep situational context and may suggest deprecated methods without warning. Their true utility is reducing initial friction, not making core architectural choices.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">Looking 5–10 years ahead</p>
              <p>Developers may converse with multi-agent pipelines that build, test, and benchmark microservices against synthetic workloads. Humans will still define objectives, enforce privacy boundaries, and resolve conflicting business constraints.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">Hot take</p>
              <p class="hot-take">“90% of current ‘AI agent’ workflows are just fragile <code>while</code> loops wrapped around regex parsers.”</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <div class="member-top">
            <img class="portrait" src="{{image:Sayemah.png}}" alt="Sayemah">
            <div>
              <h3 class="member-name">Sayemah</h3>
              <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science · 1st semester</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="member-body">
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">Into</p>
              <ul class="interest-list"><li>Calligraphy</li><li>Culinary arts &amp; cooking</li><li>Traveling</li><li>Human-computer interaction</li></ul>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">A little known fact</p>
              <p>I can master a complex traditional recipe on the first try, but one unmatched curly brace will ruin my entire evening.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">AI in engineering today</p>
              <p>AI brings creativity and swift prototyping into engineering, lowering the barrier to novel ideas. But software is also about communication and interface empathy. Current models produce functional code, which can lack aesthetic intention and elegance.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">Looking 5–10 years ahead</p>
              <p>Software design will become more human-centric and multidisciplinary. Engineers will guide agents with design systems and ethical standards, treating code generation as a utility while focusing creative energy on user delight and seamless interactions.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="member-field">
              <p class="field-label">Hot take</p>
              <p class="hot-take">“Prompt engineering is not the future of software engineering; thoughtful human design is.”</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="future-section" id="future-of-se" aria-labelledby="future-title">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="future-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">Our shared perspective</p>
          <h2 id="future-title">The Future of Software Engineering</h2>
          <p>We see AI as a powerful change to how software gets made—not a substitute for engineering judgment. The work ahead is about giving automation the right constraints, checking what it produces, and keeping people at the center of the systems we build.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="future-grid">
          <article class="future-card">
            <span class="future-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
            <h3>From typing to intent</h3>
            <p>As agents take on more boilerplate and routine implementation, engineers can spend more time defining requirements, edge cases, system boundaries, and the outcomes a product should achieve.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="future-card">
            <span class="future-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
            <h3>Verification is the craft</h3>
            <p>Generated code still needs careful review. Reliability, concurrency, security, privacy, and fault tolerance demand people who understand the system and know how to test its assumptions.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="future-card">
            <span class="future-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
            <h3>Human context matters</h3>
            <p>Good software is more than code that compiles. Accessibility, thoughtful interfaces, domain understanding, and empathy help make technical systems useful and responsible for real people.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="closing-thought">
          <p>Use AI to move faster. Keep human judgment in charge of where you’re going.</p>
          <span>Build with care</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <p>Built by an agent, supervised by humans. 2026 · Thoughtful Systems</p>
  </footer>

  <script>
    (function () {
      const button = document.getElementById("theme-toggle");
      const root = document.documentElement;

      function updateButton(theme) {
        const night = theme === "dark";
        button.textContent = night ? "☀" : "☾";
        button.setAttribute("aria-label", night ? "Switch to day mode" : "Switch to night mode");
        button.setAttribute("title", night ? "Switch to day mode" : "Switch to night mode");
      }

      updateButton(root.dataset.theme || "light");

      button.addEventListener("click", function () {
        const next = root.dataset.theme === "dark" ? "light" : "dark";
        root.dataset.theme = next;
        updateButton(next);
        try {
          localStorage.setItem("upb-theme", next);
        } catch (_) {
          /* Theme remains active for this page view if storage is unavailable. */
        }
      });
    }());
  </script>
</body>
</html>
